## ⚙️ **Scenario-Based Questions**

---

### **Scenario 1:**
**Q:** A JK Flip-Flop is toggling uncontrollably between 0 and 1 during a single clock pulse when $J=1, K=1$. What is the fix?[cite: 1]  
**A:** This is the **Race-Around Condition**[cite: 1]. Fix it by changing from level-triggered to **Edge-Triggered** or using a **Master-Slave JK configuration**[cite: 1].

---

### **Scenario 2:**
**Q:** Two specific blocks of memory keep kicking each other out of the cache, slowing down the CPU. What is wrong?[cite: 1]  
**A:** This is **Cache Thrashing** caused by **Direct Mapping**[cite: 1]. Fix it by upgrading to a **Set-Associative** cache mapping[cite: 1].

---

### **Scenario 3:**
**Q:** You need a circuit that takes a 3-bit code from a TV remote to route a single input video signal to one of 8 screens. What do you use?[cite: 1]  
**A:** Use a **1-to-8 Demultiplexer (Demux)**[cite: 1]. The video is the input, and the 3-bit code controls which screen gets the signal[cite: 1].
